tƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkf200000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AJM7kcfDaZbTVMs9BClq1Q-K0d8x4tHJVwFta3oV8VIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarks0.34192290000000003ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;nzXYKornp9i2zg9cnLyYu4LvqzZ4WkKqYsjPgqbKzbsƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka3ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-n9ReIjwA4VKVzjkjijdOZY-DKAZBIDMOQDnmcdEn28ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke32000ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;kxln4qtNXavXZQlgzPcGz-7d-AG6BmsG7ycj37_YO6Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarke10267ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;okQ2H3JKUjJvVsyUCsWoz63zLnFSA9NGKVYwXFotSQAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka0ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;PjkPVu7ZavAzQe6GhbaD4XEMjIBNYy4wHpcsG-MoWHQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarka3ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;qXi_zQ6D9K8igeBxPPfrnFKYMQN0rKOSKLtNLDltticƒdpairƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;tDP5wFwfNCbZxjjceezTwi2VeSng7IWsmRP5PKOm61Eƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky¿{"tool":"submit_revision_request","failureLayer":"writer-model","replayFrom":"Repair description, summary metadata, and tighten final section's CONTEXT 1 usage to one attributed fact.","summary":"The body prose is solid and well-attributed but two metadata fieldsâ€”description and summaryâ€”fail form requirements, and the final section draws more than one attributed fact from a supporting context item. Bounded repairs make the manuscript publishable.","requiredRepairs":["Description field must include the analytical frame. Current text ('Spain face Argentina in the FIFA World Cup final this Sunday at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey.') is a bare event statement (~80 characters) with no hook. Per the form exemplar, the description targets approximately 113 characters and must convey the article's geometry/space-control angle so a reader knows why to click.","Summary field must be trimmed to approximately 53 words across three sentences (the event, the key numbers or development, the frame). The current summary runs approximately 84 wordsâ€”nearly double the targetâ€”and must be compressed without losing the geometry thesis.","The 'What Argentina must answer' section opens with two distinct attributed facts from CONTEXT 1 (Argentina's compact-defense/counter-attack model; their semi-final win over England). The context-usage rule permits one explicitly attributed fact per context item; anchor the section's opening in a single attributed sentence from CONTEXT 1 and pivot immediately to THE STORY's own concluding observation about Argentina studying Spain's tactics."],"report":"**Body prose audit â€” PASS**\n\nAttribution is visible and consistent throughout. Every key factual claim traces to a licensed source via inline link: Spain's 2-0 win over France from THE STORY; the Porro 58th-minute goal linked to AP News as cited in THE STORY; the MbappÃ© \"lack of communication\" quote attributed and linked to the Reuters source named in THE STORY; the Nature player-tracking research and the PLOS ONE passing-network research both linked exactly as they appear in the source text. The PLOS ONE DOI suffix `10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0171156` is reproduced faithfully in the URL (the faithfulness-gate number). No invented events, quotes, numbers, people, or causal mechanisms appear. The triangles-in-basketball analogy (Phil Jackson, 1987â€“1998, Tex Winter's triangle offence, Chicago Bulls) is drawn directly from THE STORY without embellishment. The lede names the event concretely in its first sentence and the demand lens (geometry, space, football, final) is expressed naturally throughout the body rather than forced. The \"will\" prohibition is respected: the body uses \"may\" and \"could\" rather than \"will\" for forward-looking statements. No rhetorical questions appear. The ending opens outward without predicting. The \"As [X] notes/reports\" template is used twice, within the permitted limit, with varied constructions elsewhere.\n\n**Headline â€” PASS**\n\nThe headline carries the source article's own organizing terms and is produced by the `source-title-fallback` mechanism, which is appropriate and faithful.\n\n**Lede â€” PASS**\n\nThe lede (one paragraph, approximately 90 words) names the event, venue, and stakes in the first sentence, then establishes the analytical question the article develops. Acceptable.\n\n**Section structure â€” PASS WITH NOTE**\n\nFour sections build a single analysis: the geometry of the semi-final triangles, the probabilistic space model, the cross-sport triangle principle, and what the analysis implies for Argentina. Each section continues the prior argument without restating the event. The demand-lens warning (`demand-lens-missing-h2`) from the deterministic standards is acknowledged; \"The shape that conquered basketball\" signals the geometry frame through \"shape\" and \"A pitch made of probabilities\" signals the spatial/quantitative frame. The warning does not rise to a required repair on its own.\n\n**Material failures requiring revision**\n\n*Description field.* The current value is: \"Spain face Argentina in the FIFA World Cup final this Sunday at MetLife Stadium in New Jersey.\" This is approximately 80 characters and carries no analytical hook. The form exemplar targets approximately 113 characters and requires the description to convey the article's distinctive angle â€” here, Spain's geometric space-control system and what it means for the final. A reader seeing this description in a feed or search result learns nothing that distinguishes this article from any match preview. This is a material metadata defect.\n\n*Summary field.* The current summary runs approximately 84 words across three sentences. The form requirement specifies approximately 53 words. The third sentence (recording both sides' rankings and titles) is factually accurate but padds the count, and the second sentence can be tightened. Trimming to target does not require removing the article's key analytical points.\n\n*Final section context usage.* \"What Argentina must answer\" opens with two distinct attributed facts drawn from CONTEXT 1 â€” Argentina's tactical identity (compact defense, rapid counter-attack through Messi) and their semi-final win over England â€” before pivoting to THE STORY's concluding observation. The pipeline instruction limits a context item to \"one explicitly attributed fact or comparison.\" Two attributed facts from one context item in a single section gives that item more structural weight than the rule permits. This is repairable by compressing the Argentina tactical description into a single attributed sentence and moving immediately to THE STORY's geometry conclusion.\n\n**Fairness, harm, sensationalism â€” PASS**\n\nThe article does not criticize a person or institution, allege wrongdoing, or report a dispute requiring a response opportunity. No needless harm, stereotyping, or commercial influence is detected. Reported analysis is distinct from advocacy throughout.\n\n**Failure layer diagnosis**\n\nThe assignment, sources, and instructions were sufficient to produce a publishable manuscript. The body prose demonstrates this. The description and summary failures are execution errors against explicit form requirements stated in the prompt; the context-usage issue in the final section is an execution error against an explicit sourcing rule. Both are writer-model failures, not upstream defects in assignment or sources. A targeted replay of the three identified repairs produces a publishable manuscript without any structural changes to the body."}ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;ylUi8PuO7Wb5_fJggwv8FYOohp4I-YQn971jl-tVZPYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx$f34c2c25-95d0-42a5-9bc8-0285ee6793cfƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;D3ImzyaIq6A3HcDzJuF6euM-NudwuuB2CS0cMz7Fwzgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkhtool_useƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;J5ZxINyPoNrxXGTaJibLPvqoKaPUOmPNt8LhRu6w-60ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KY_u7MPKR7xX0tecLDBGrhRQMXZ0Zt69adTrXeOMlRYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarklwriter-modelƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;VgWuvi-qmO5SXSi6bMBFEzTDOqDYNicgLpvMPkundLEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxiRepair description, summary metadata, and tighten final section's CONTEXT 1 usage to one attributed fact.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;0gD9-EQtof3_ZsO6S53B95GaGLpXisevsCmfw84icLUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkyI**Body prose audit â€” PASS**

