ll-and-the-world-cup-final:3] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Attacking flair and physicality will no doubt play a role. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:4] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: But we could also see an underappreciated element of football come to the fore: geometry . (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n- reported-development: advance distinct reported details without restating the frame\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:5] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: In their 2-0 World Cup semi-final win over France , Spain formed neat passing triangles around the French players. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:6] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: This sometimes made it look as if Spain had extra people on the field. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:7] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Wherever a Spanish player received the ball, two teammates appeared at different angles â€“ with their French opponents seemingly always arriving a fraction too late. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:8] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: The triangle mattered not because it was neat, but because it gave Spain choice and France uncertainty. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:9] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Each pass forced a French defender to commit to one possible future: press the ball, block the inside route, or protect the space behind. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n- affected-actors-and-response: develop the reported effects, named actors, and institutional response without inventing connective tissue\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:10] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: By the time that choice was made, the ball had often moved and the geometry had changed again. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:11] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Spain were not simply finding space. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:12] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: They were controlling when and where the next space would appear. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:13] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Forcing choices Put three attackers in a straight line and one defender can often block both supporting players. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:14] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: But move one supporting player sideways and the passing lines separate. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n- consequences-and-open-status: close on the most consequential source-supported unresolved fact, decision, deadline, conflict, or question\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:15] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: The defender must choose which route to close. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:16] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Press the ball and a pass can go around them. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:17] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Protect the inside route and the outside may open. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:18] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: If another defender steps across, a Spanish player can attack the space left behind. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:19] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: A useful football triangle does not need equal sides or 60-degree angles. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\n  - [claim:geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final:20] Geometry, football and the World Cup final: Its best shape changes with defendersâ€™ positions, body orientation, ball speed and the space available. (attribute: https://theconversation.com/geometry-football-and-the-world-cup-final-287792)\nCommission-specific writing law:\n- Be lively without laundering rumor into fact or manufacturing conflict, intimacy, scandal, or certainty.\n- Attribute claims about relationships, health, private conduct, wrongdoing, or disputed statements to the exact admitted source.\n- Do not confuse publicity material, fan speculation, anonymous social posts, and independent reporting.\n- Give the audience the promised factual payoff; curiosity may organize the headline but may not replace the answer.\nInterpretation law: systems interpretation may organize supported assertions but may not supply facts, causes, motives, consequences, trends, or analogies\nPROHIBITED: do not 