Cup final: the referee, the stats and the omens","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/19/spain-v-argentina-world-cup-final-referee-stats-omens","domain":"theguardian.com","published":"Sun, 19 Jul 2026 07:00:21 GMT","assertedAt":"2026-07-19T15:58:02.610Z","score":25,"matchedTerms":["football","cup","final"],"summary":"<p>As the top two in the Fifa rankings prepare to meet in New Jersey on Sunday we look at the pointers that may help decide the game</p><p>Slavko Vincic becomes the first Slovene to referee a World Cup final. He oversaw the 2024 Champions League final at Wembley (Real Madrid beat Borussia Dortmund 2-0) as well as Spainâ€™s 2-1 win over France at the 2024 Euros semi-final. The 46-year-oldâ€™s first World Cup match was Argentinaâ€™s opening loss to Saudi Arabia in 2022. At this tournament, Vincic showed Ecuadorâ€™s Piero HincapiÃ© a red card for covering his mouth in the 95th minute against Mexico. He has averaged 2.33 yellow cards per game.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul..."},{"kind":"producing-content.farm.research-packet.source","subject":"rifts-began-to-appear-why-many-latin-americans-want-spain-to-beat-argentina-in-the-world-cup-final","wire":"sports","title":"â€˜Rifts began to appearâ€™: Why many Latin Americans want Spain to beat Argentina in the World Cup final","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/jul/18/argentina-spain-latin-america-support-world-cup-final","domain":"theguardian.com","published":"Sat, 18 Jul 2026 15:03:00 GMT","assertedAt":"2026-07-19T15:58:02.610Z","score":25,"matchedTerms":["football","cup","final"],"summary":"<p>A history of racism and ongoing footballing rivalries have made the choice of which team to get behind in Sundayâ€™s final a charged topic</p><p>The Brazilian journalist and columnist Julia Duailibi usually writes about politics in her weekly column for the leading Brazilian newspaper O Globo, but last Thursday she took a different tack, writing instead about wh